{# THE ORGANISATION DASHBOARD'S WIDGET LIBRARY — chrome around the shell's
   shared preset component.

   Design: widgets.html in the design workspace.

   NOTHING ORGANISATION-SHAPED HAPPENS INSIDE THAT COMPONENT: it is handed
   this surface's catalogue, this surface's partial name and this surface's
   routes, and it renders the strips, the toolbar and the canvas. Arranging
   this dashboard works exactly as arranging any other in the installation,
   which is the whole reason this page rides the framework rather than
   carrying a copy of it.

   THE SECTIONS ARE THE CONTRIBUTORS, NOT DESIGN DIRECTIONS. A person needs to
   know that "Patrols out right now" came from the patrols module, so that the
   day it is uninstalled its disappearance reads as the system working rather
   than as a bug. The five directions the page was drawn in are the PRESETS. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}The organisation &middot; widget library{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\ShellBundle\\ShellBundle::WIDGET_STYLESHEET')) }}">
    {% for sheet in moduleStylesheets %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(sheet) }}">
    {% endfor %}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_tabs %}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ urls.dashboard }}">{{ shell_brand().name|lower }}</a> / widget library
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}The organisation &middot; widget library{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    What <a href="{{ urls.dashboard }}">the dashboard</a> is composed from. Adopt one of the five compositions
    this installation ships, or compose your own &mdash; every widget is the real thing at full size, and every
    one of them names the module it came from.
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    <form method="post" action="{{ urls.reset }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
        <button type="submit" class="tgl w-act">{{ ux_icon('shell:rotate-ccw') }} Reset to defaults</button>
    </form>
    <a class="cta" href="{{ urls.dashboard }}">{{ ux_icon('shell:chevron-left') }} Back to the dashboard</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {{ include('@Shell/widget/_library.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}
